WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.680
Press two films together and pull them apart, and electricity flows. The team 3D printed the top film.

2
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:15.880
Plain PVDF is dominated by a phase where molecular dipoles pair up in opposite directions and cancel out, so its output was weak.

3
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:27.080
Perovskite nanoparticles were mixed into the ink, printed, and heat treated. Polar crystals in the film increased, and the surface opened up pores that gather charge.

4
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.000
The share of the polar crystal phase rose from about 45 to 88 percent.

5
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:44.780
Pressed with the same force, the voltage rose from 80 to 392 volts, about five times. It lit 200 LEDs and stayed stable over eighteen thousand presses.

6
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:52.860
It picked up signals from feet and wrists and mapped touch on a robot hand, pointing toward wearables powered by motion.
